# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Inventory folders.** [init.py](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/init.py) calls [build_dev_inventory_matrix](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/builder.py), which creates one folder per round at `<inventory-dir>-<round>` (or just `<inventory-dir>` when there is a single round). For each folder, `build_dev_inventory` resolves the round's per-app variant payload and bakes it into the inventory's `host_vars` as `applications.<app>: <variant-payload>` overrides. The inventory is therefore variant-resolved on disk; no runtime selector is needed."
msgstr "**Pastas de inventário.** [init.py](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/init.py) chamadas [build_dev_inventory_matrix](../../../cli/administration/deploy/development/inventory/builder.py), que cria uma pasta por rodada em `<inventory-dir>-<round>` (ou apenas `<inventory-dir>` quando há uma única rodada). Para cada pasta, `build_dev_inventory` resolve a carga útil variante da rodada por aplicativo e assa-a no inventário `host_vars` como `applications.<app>: <variant-payload>` Ativações. O inventário é, portanto, resolvido pela variante no disco; nenhum seletor de tempo de execução é necessário."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Inventory pin**: set `test_e2e_playwright_keep: \"true\"` in `group_vars` or `host_vars` of the target environment."
msgstr "**Pino de inventário**: set `test_e2e_playwright_keep: \"true\"` em `group_vars` ou `host_vars` do ambiente-alvo."

