# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy com auto-fornecimento:** V1 portas todo o acesso através do compartilhado Keycloak Cliente OIDC (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty encaminha a identidade autenticada para n8n como um confiável `Remote-Email` cabeçalho (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); a `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adaptado de [PavelSozonov/n8n-comunidade-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) lê esse cabeçalho, auto- fornece um n local8n usuário no primeiro login, e problemas n8cookie de sessão própria de n - assim cada Keycloak usuário pousa diretamente no editor de fluxo de trabalho, sem segundo, n8passo de login n-local."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via oauth2-proxy com auto-fornecimento:** V1 portas todo o acesso através do compartilhado Keycloak Cliente OIDC (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty encaminha a identidade autenticada para n8n como um confiável ``Remote-Email`` cabeçalho (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); a ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adaptado de `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) lê esse cabeçalho, auto- fornece um n local8n usuário no primeiro login, e problemas n8cookie de sessão própria de n - assim cada Keycloak usuário pousa diretamente no editor de fluxo de trabalho, sem segundo, n8passo de login n-local."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** é SuiteCRMlogin de SAML próprio contra Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` em [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), não um proxy na frente dele. Pedidos não autenticados atingiram o ponto de entrada SAML do firewall Symfony, que redireciona para Keycloak; a asserção volta a `/saml/acs` e estabelece um real SuiteCRM sessão, então o aplicativo renderiza sua própria UI autenticada, incluindo seu controle de logout. As contas são criadas no primeiro login da asserção (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), e o certificado de assinatura IdP é lido de Keycloakdescritor de reino por [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) no arranque, sobre o proxy Tor SOCKS sempre que o emissor é uma cebola, porque um `.onion` O emitente é irresolvível diretamente. `/auth` permanece acessível como o login local de vidro de ruptura."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** é SuiteCRMlogin SAML próprio contra Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` em ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` permanece acessível como o login local de vidro de ruptura."

